# THE LAMP POOL GOES TO THE FRAME (15_lights.pool_before): the web tier lights
# only a few sources, so they go to what is on screen first, then to what only
# spills in, and by distance within each. `perf lights` prints every candidate,
# its tier and whether it got a light: a source in frame (tier 0) left dark
# while one out of frame is POOLED is the failure. Which sources get the slots
# never changes the light STATE, so on the web no program is first drawn after
# either event. Frames: 01 the burning at dusk, 02 a village house at night,
# the pair the web's lamp dimming is judged on against the desktop's.
#
#   tools/web.sh --tour=tours/lamp-pool.tour --programs --args=--seed=7,--weather=clear:0
#   tools/tour.sh tours/lamp-pool.tour --seed=7 --weather=clear:0
coast calm
hour 19.5
place burning
wait 2.0
echo event dusk
wait 1.0
perf lights
shot 01-burning-dusk with land:burning
hour 23
place coast
near house
wait 2.0
echo event night
wait 1.0
perf lights
shot 02-village-night with land:coast
